<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The global economy faces the prospect of $=
100 a barrel oil again, as the conflict in the Middle East continues.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Brent crude has risen back over the $98 a =
barrel mark already this week, its highest level since 24 July. Oil has bee=
n pushed up by reports that Yemen=E2=80=99s Iran-aligned Houthis attacked e=
nergy facilities in Saudi Arabia.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Saudi authorities said operations at some =
energy facilities had been halted today following attacks =E2=80=8Cby Yemen=
=E2=80=99s Iran-aligned Houthis that wounded more than 70 people.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The attacks add to the pressure on oil and=
 gas production in the region, which remains badly disrupted by the ongoing=
 Iran war.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Yesterday, the Financial Times reported th=
at Saudi Aramco=E2=80=99s oil facilities in the Saudi Arabian city of Jizan=
 =E2=80=93 where one of the country=E2=80=99s largest refineries is based =
=E2=80=93 have been attacked</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Earlier today, Iran threatened to create a=
 new restricted zone in the Gulf if the US pressed on with its =E2=80=9Ceco=
nomic warfare=E2=80=9D against Tehran.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Such a zone would, presumably, further und=
ermine US efforts to reopen the strait of Hormuz.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Mohsen Rezaei, the secretary of Iran=E2=80=
=99s Supreme National Security Council, said Iran had=E2=80=9C fundamentall=
y recalibrated=E2=80=9D its posture towards US forces.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Rezaei posted on X: =E2=80=9CIn recent day=
s, Washington has received a clear warning from Iran=E2=80=99s new missiles=
. Economic warfare will be met by a maritime exclusion zone across the Pers=
ian Gulf to the blockade perimeter. The operational posture toward U.S. war=
ships and bases has been fundamentally recalibrated.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Shipping traffic through the strait of Hor=
muz has already slowed this week =E2=80=93 just seven commodity vessels sai=
ling through the passage on Monday, down from eight on Sunday. Before the w=
ar began, about 130 ships a day would cross the strait.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">This is all a headache for central bankers=
, as high oil prices create inflationary pressures through the economy. Lat=
er today, MPs in London will question <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.t=
heguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEDZQCxC_1=
9XC5K9o6Guywi2XfQRKl-bZFWD75QT87Mj7nbAJsAwfC4_2XWFEQ5rYnrT-_tuNrv3Xkx_Tq5AK=
4iVBwmDFRDut34wUWBoMSuB4C8psBYrmwO2lk2rZeyM3Mh8x1982dcD5mtpFowXnxgbUx1LGb2N=
55JLhSrccrkxvcceQoTSJWYnYepR5NH2nTnxN639Nmwig4P2N4JS4_tQ/4tv/DsVo9XyFTHanIq=
b1QgmFDQ/h31/h001.2UMPzLKvoXxpMU7N-19z26nXBbJv3qKi-xo5FVVZBoE" style=3D"col=
or: #0077B6;">Bank of England</a> governor Andrew Bailey, and colleagues, a=
bout their recent decision to hold the Bank rate at 3.75%.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">MPs are likely to question witnesses on th=
e potential inflationary impact of the ongoing war in Iran and how the MPC =
considers recent developments in AI, the committee says.<strong><br><br></s=
trong></p>
